# bashmemo usage
# Create or edit a memo:
# @@ mymemo
# Write one command per line, then save and quit your editor.
# List all memos:
# @
# Load a memo and add its commands to history:
# @ mymemo
# Search memos by name prefix:
# @ my
# View a memo without adding anything to history:
# @ -v mymemo
# @v mymemo
# Append the previous history entry to a memo:
# @+ mymemo
# Append a specific history entry number to a memo:
# @+ mymemo 100
# Use the Up arrow or Ctrl+R after loading a memo to recall, edit, and run commands.
# Memo names cannot contain / or wildcards, and cannot start with -.
# Set MEMOFILES_DIR to store memos outside this repository, and EDITOR to choose the editor used by @@.
